WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.170
February 26th (Thursday)

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.180
Yuki-chan.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.720
Touya-kun.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.480
We're almost there.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.660
There is one thing you can do.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.250
You understand, right?

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.070
I'll help, too.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.560
Good luck

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.560
Yuki

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.530
nemuri nasai ima wa tada

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.530
Sleep, for now

00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:01.410
watashi no naka de doko ni mo ikanai de

00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:01.410
Inside of me, and don't go anywhere

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:22.460
madoromi no fuchi de yureteru gunjou iro no yo

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:22.460
Through the slumbering ultramarine sky

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.940
majiwaru koto no nai hoshi wo sagashiteru

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.940
I am searching for stars that will never cross

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:35.670
anata wo motomeru yubisaki yami ni samayotte

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:35.670
These fingertips search for you, but are lost in darkness

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:44.540
mogaite mo nukedesenai ai no umi ni oboreteku

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:44.540
I try but I can't escape, and I drown in the sea of love

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:52.450
yawaranai toiki ni kokoro sae mo furueru

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:52.450
Your tender sigh makes my heart tremble

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:58.050
karamaru utsukushi kumo no ito no you

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:58.050
Seemingly entangled in the beautiful strands of a spider web

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:02.560
ugokenai no watashi wo yurushite

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:02.560
I cannot move, please forgive me

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.850
anata no ude ni dakarete nemuru

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.850
I am sleeping with your arms around me

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.110
nani mo kamo sutetatte ii

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.110
I don't mind losing anything else

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:16.610
ii kono mama no maboroshi nante zukuru no wa yamete

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:16.610
Stop pretending that you are a good girl

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:20.110
hontou no watashi wo mitsukete

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:20.110
Find the real me

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:26.170
zutto matteru

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:26.170
I'll be waiting forever

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.850
Last night, the singer Ogata Rina collapsed

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.390
at her workplace, the Touou Television studios,

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:35.090
after drinking tea containing poison.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:36.840
She was rushed to the Municipal Hospital.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.990
According to the examination results, her life does not seem to be in danger.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:44.340
The police are currently investigating whether this incident was accidental or intentional.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:47.500
Page 25
It's someone else's fault.
It's not my fault.
It's all someone else's fault.
None of it is my-

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.700
Yuki

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.330
Yuki

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.290
It's you she wants.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.340
Don't cry

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.210
I'm... sorry...

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:53.240
But, Rina-chan...

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.130
I feel so sorry for you...

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.310
Don't pity me

00:03:58.480 --> 00:03:59.530
It's someone else's problem

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.450
Do you really have the time to worry about this?

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:09.120
The contest isn't over

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:19.250
I'll definitely get better before the real show

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.810
The doctor said that rather than poison,

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:33.150
it was detergent, bleach, or something of the sort.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:36.850
Since there wasn't very much of it, it wasn't life-threatening.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.980
Help came quickly, too.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.520
The guard who just happened to be
walking by quickly reported the incident.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:45.280
Her throat does seem to be affected,

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.750
but not to the point where she wouldn't be able to use her voice.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:50.900
It's probably due to psychological shock.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.190
Where's Ei-chan?

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.650
He's been at the police station since last night.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.090
He... turned himself in?

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:01.340
I see.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:05.010
Now these misunderstandings can be cleared,

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:07.070
and things should settle down for you guys.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.570
If only that were so.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.690
I'm going to talk with the police.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.460
What a face.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.690
It's going to affect your next event.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.640
I'll go to the bathroom.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.940
How convenient.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:45.180
Congratulations.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.490
I lost.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:50.120
Feel free to do whatever you want from now on.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.180
Then, Yuki...

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:55.480
Yes, there's no need to worry anymore.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.580
Is it fine to leave her alone?

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.220
Fujii-san.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:03.270
Last night, when Yuki-san went to you...

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:05.800
You didn't respond to her.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.730
You didn't help her.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.470
That's because...

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.420
... Menou-san was there?

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.020
Or was it because she had been with Ogata-san?

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.270
Yuki-san needs you, Fujii-san.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:21.000
That's because

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.000
Yuki, she

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:24.280
You're no longer a hindrance to her.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.170
Am I right?

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:32.440
It seems my plans have failed.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:37.570
The reason I approached you, Fujii-san,

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:41.630
is because those who love me will eventually disappear.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:45.300
As long as I can remain by Yuki's side,

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.830
nobody would be able to approach-

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:49.720
I've never loved you.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:51.810
That's right.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:54.260
You've never loved anyone.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:56.390
Apart from Yuki?

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.390
You don't know how to love.

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:56.390
Or could it be

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.560
How do you know?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.590
That's because...

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.460
You've fallen in love with me?

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:02.560
Not at all.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.640
I hate you.

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.360
I've always hated you.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.220
Even now.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:08.510
Good.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.760
This is meaningless at this point.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.070
Are you sad?

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:25.070
No.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.830
Why do you ask?

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.110
Sorry for the wait!

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.410
Excuse me.

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:43.710
That's good.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.940
I'm sorry this came late.

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:06.140
Farewell

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:06.670
Shinozuka-san

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.840
You want me to look for the culprit?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.390
Actually, why do I even have to do it?

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:14.390
Isn't this a job for the police?

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:16.790
Why do you keep investigating mysteries?

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:17.850
It's my hobby.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:20.120
Then take it as a hobby or whatever,

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.150
and help me think about this.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:24.030
If we know who did it,

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:25.380
then it just might...

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.820
help Rina-chan's recovery a little.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:32.130
Isn't that the doctor's job?

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:35.080
I just wanted to thank my savior-goddess...

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:35.920
One last time.

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.670
So it's that, after all.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.560
Ah, I understand now.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:44.200
Already?

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:45.110
Who?

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:47.360
No, I'm not talking about the culprit.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.360
Though, the culprit's probably one of the employees.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.240
He'd have to know when Ogata Rina's alone,

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:54.680
and what she drinks in order to do that.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.960
Otherwise, he'd never be able to even get close to her,

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:58.700
let alone poison her drink.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.920
Is that so?

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:03.480
I should've been there with her, then...

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.740
That's right.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:06.090
It's your fault.

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:10.020
... though, I don't really believe that.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:12.360
You wanted Mocha?

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:12.990
No.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:15.310
Eh... so, Kilimanjaro?

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:16.760
Or maybe Blue Mountain?

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:17.960
I didn't order anything.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.750
How about having coffee with the chocolate Yuki gave you?

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:26.850
It'll be good.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.520
I'll also take the opportunity to try some of it...

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.550
What was it you understood before?

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:43.600
Matsuyama Menou knew Yuki.

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.520
Well, everyone does.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.430
That's not what I meant.

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:55.180
She knew her long before Yuki even debuted.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:58.000
When you met Matsuyama Menou,

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.510
if Yuki was there with you,

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:02.300
would it have resulted in a love triangle?

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:03.700
Stop fooling around.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:05.900
I met Yuki during high school.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:08.050
Menou wasn't one of your seniors?

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.660
If she was, you'd know her too, right?

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:15.800
Plus, Menou-san's quite a bit older than us.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:18.560
I'd say about four or five years older?

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.190
Then, it must've been when you were a kid, huh?

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:25.140
Didn't she say you were little?

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:30.410
I already said that I'd never met Yuki when I was a kid.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:33.780
If I did, then when we entered high school,

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:36.330
Haruka would've said from the very beginning,

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:38.090
"Ah, Yuki."

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:42.260
That's true.

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:45.220
But, if it's Haruka you're talking about,

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:46.350
because it's Haruka...

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.300
Whatever.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:50.300
What do you mean, "whatever"?

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:54.300
It doesn't matter anymore where I've met Menou-san before.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.400
Touya, you...

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:00.940
I know who I really am.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.400
People really won't recognize who I am...

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:58.490
... if I use this disguise!

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:02.460
You taught me something useful.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:07.110
Apparently, Ei-chan's at the police station now.

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:11.750
He's got to make this clear.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.120
You hate indecision, right?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.550
Based on some tip-offs,

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:21.780
both the police and the mass media believe it's Misumi's doing, after all.

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:23.410
He's cornered all right.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:28.060
He seems to have taken several paintings and concealed their whereabouts.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.980
It looked like he'd already decided to leave our company long ago.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:34.080
I'm sorry

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:35.760
What are you saying?

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.320
You're one of the victims.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.450
I'm the one who should be apologizing.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:43.360
I couldn't protect my own artists.  I'm a useless proprietor.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:53.290
I'll admit this.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:57.320
I used a painting my husband left me after we divorced,

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.460
with the intention to take over Ogata Productions.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.370
For him to childishly take the bait so quickly...

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.240
Ei-chan's too innocent.

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:09.860
What's more, he went as far as selling his own sister.

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:12.060
It's all my fault.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:16.490
Even if this scandal never existed, my company wouldn't have lasted.

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:20.860
I was hoping that you and Menou could hold us out a little longer,

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:21.830
but Menou...

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.710
My own daughter... made me realize I was wrong all along.

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:28.410
Rina-san.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.080
I'm sorry for having deceived you.

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:40.120
I'm going back to the office.

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:46.090
You know,

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:49.760
I've never told anyone about my relationship with Menou.

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:52.930
I have no idea what she's planning.

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:06.330
I'll have to start over, but...

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.510
That's exactly what I needed!

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:11.890
President Kanzaki!

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:12.500
Excuse me-

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:13.660
What is Rina-san's condition-

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:14.270
Wait-

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:15.610
And President Ogata?

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:17.060
About the dubbing-

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:18.240
Where's Menou-san?

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.920
Say something-

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.050
The culprit?

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:22.390
Please!

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.120
Ah, you're awake.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:03.920
This?

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.510
Or this?

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:26.070
Was it a gold coin you lost?

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:28.770
Or was it a silver coin?

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:30.590
Or could it be...

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.140
... this?

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:47.630
You'll forget everything if you eat that.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:50.590
Everything bad.

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:56.910
I'll protect you from now on.

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:59.810
I'll be beside you, appearing differently each time,

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:04.090
so that no matter when, I'll still be your savior-goddess.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:16.550
Have you been watching me since then?

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:18.820
Nope.

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:21.410
I completely disappeared from your life, didn't I?

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:23.310
You did.

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:26.410
There's no way I could've possibly watched out for you every day.

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:30.090
I thought I'd just say it, and for the moment leave it.

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:34.130
But then, I got busy myself.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:39.650
Problems came up with my family, and I couldn't keep it up.

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:40.510
Okay.

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:46.090
I'll be honest.  I forgot.

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:50.570
When I met you at Koukai Street...

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:56.500
The moment I saw you, I was like, "Ah, it's that kid".

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.620
And then it was like, boom boom boom.

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:02.070
Is that what they call a near-death experience?

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:06.080
I thought I was gonna die.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:09.220
After that, I got seriously shocked.

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:12.560
I'm

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:14.530
curse

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:14.530
savior-goddess

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:12.510
I would've never imagined that one phrase could have such an effect.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:14.530
I'll protect you

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:14.530
no matter when

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:14.530
appearing differently

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:14.530
binding
 curse

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:14.530
I'm your savior-goddess

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:14.530
savior-goddess

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:14.530
savior-goddess

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:17.490
Savior-goddess

00:17:18.820 --> 00:17:21.030
That was... how it started.

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:22.180
Yep.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:25.980
Then, is it right to say I'm made of savior-goddesses?

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:26.940
How?

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:31.700
The savior-goddesses that have appeared in front of me, up until now...

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:34.390
They're all coincidences.

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:36.910
What's more, they're nothing but your own impressions.

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:48.110
Actually, that was what I wanted to say,

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:51.130
but you also have your own reasons, don't you?

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:54.130
My eyes have not been blinded.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.590
Yuki's beyond my predicting, though.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:00.730
Why are you so disappointed?!

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:03.400
Don't you have many wonderful memories?

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:05.650
Since you were just a little kid, too.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:08.950
Ouch...

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:09.920
Your thanks?

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:13.940
I did it all for you, you know.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:15.900
Exposing my past...

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.990
Revealing that my singing was dubbed...

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:22.530
Was it really... all for my sake?

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:26.560
Please.

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:28.720
You'll be hurt.

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:31.020
I'm used to that.

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:33.190
I've already suffered so much.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:37.640
It's my turn to ask you.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:41.780
What were you looking for at the time?

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:42.750
Dunno.

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:49.690
Menou's here, isn't she?

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:51.650
President...

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:55.410
Yayoi-chan told me.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:56.190
Stop her.

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:02.750
Let me... go!

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:04.980
Let me go!  Let go of me!

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:08.490
Give it up!

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:15.990
Cheap wine again.

00:19:15.990 --> 00:19:19.140
It's times like this that second-rate wine is best.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:21.270
Get me a glass.

00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:21.990
Huh?

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:25.370
Get me a teacup or something, hurry up!

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:27.180
O-Okay.

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:32.660
It'll be perfect for listening to your confessions.

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:34.070
As for the refreshment...

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.030
This is who you are right now.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.780
It was also the me up until now.

00:19:57.190 --> 00:19:58.120
Fujii-kun.

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:02.090
Could you keep Rina-chan company tomorrow?

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:06.100
She doesn't seem to have given up yet, but...

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:44.440
February 28th (Saturday)

00:20:44.920 --> 00:20:48.120
I'll be back tonight. Menou

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:04.450
Regarding the Ogata Rina-san poisoning case.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:06.320
This morning,

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:09.410
the police arrested one of the managers of Ogata Productions,

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:13.370
the 28-year-old Makoto Sendou, without resistance.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:15.870
The following is the verbal account of the informer who secured his arrest.

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:23.760
I happened to see him sneaking into the break room at the time.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:29.350
As one of her fans, I cannot forgive such a treacherous crime!

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:57.230
Venus Music Festival

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:01.610
It started

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:04.630
What started?

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:07.860
Venus

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:10.100
So, it's already time?

00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:16.240
You're fine with not going?

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:16.010
I'm not going.

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:18.150
Rina-chan.

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:21.100
I can't go anywhere.

00:22:23.790 --> 00:22:27.080
Now, let's have Morikawa Yuki sing for us.

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:30.730
The song is "Koiiro Sora".

00:22:49.470 --> 00:22:56.010
watashi ni itsumo anata wa yasashii

00:22:49.470 --> 00:22:56.010
You have always been kind to me

00:22:56.940 --> 00:23:02.580
sono yasashisa ga fuan ni suru

00:22:56.940 --> 00:23:02.580
But this kindness makes me insecure

00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:11.420
unmei no ito hodokenai you ni

00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:11.420
This string of fate, I'll retie it over and over

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:18.030
nando mo musubi naoshite

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:18.030
So that it will never come loose

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:26.400
tsugi ni au yakusoku dekinai mama

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:26.400
I don't want to hear you say goodbye

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:36.350
wakare no kotoba mada kikitaku wa nai yo

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:36.350
Until we make promises to meet again

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:44.090
aenai yoru ni yume de aetara

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:44.090
Even if we can't meet tonight, 
if I can see you in my dreams

00:23:44.490 --> 00:23:52.000
ashita ga tsurakute mo waratte irareru

00:23:44.490 --> 00:23:52.000
Even if tomorrow is difficult I'll be able to smile

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:59.470
donna ni tooku hanarete ite mo

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:59.470
No matter how far apart we may become

00:23:59.740 --> 00:24:09.450
tsunagatte ireru to shinjite iru

00:23:59.740 --> 00:24:09.450
I believe that we will still be connected together

00:24:21.880 --> 00:24:23.220
Page 26

00:24:24.870 --> 00:24:27.920
We are sitting together.

00:24:27.920 --> 00:24:29.260
For the whole night,

00:24:29.260 --> 00:24:30.860
we did not move.

00:24:31.830 --> 00:24:33.120
White Album.
